feat(cli): let resume choose the model it comes back with

A session stores the model it was using, and resuming was stuck with it: the only
way to change it was to start the session and type `/model`. `run` takes
`--model`, so a person expects `resume` to take it too, and being refused where
the other command accepts was a trap.

The override goes through `SetModel`, the same request the interactive command
sends, so the session's own rules judge it: a model it cannot honour is reported
with a reason instead of being half-applied. `--provider` is not needed, because
a `provider/model` reference already names the provider.
